#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:68
msgid "The configure hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:70
msgid ""
"The `configure` hook is called every time one the following actions happen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:72
msgid "initial snap installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:73
msgid "snap refresh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:74
msgid ""
"whenever the user runs `snap set|unset` to change a configuration option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:76
msgid ""
"ⓘ Note that this hook will *not* get called when the snap *itself* changes "
"configuration options using `snapctl get|set|unset`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:78
msgid ""
"The hook should use `snapctl get` to retrieve configuration values from "
"snapd. If the hook exits with a non-zero status code, the configuration will "
"not be applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:80
msgid "For example, given the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:82
msgid "$ snap set mysnap username=foo password=bar\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:86
msgid ""
"The `configure` hook located within the _mysnap_ snap at `meta/hooks/"
"configure` would be called to apply the configuration changes, if necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:88
msgid "The hook might look similar to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:90
msgid ""
"#!/bin/sh -e\n"
"\n"
"username=\"$(snapctl get username)\"\n"
"password=\"$(snapctl get password)\"\n"
"\n"
"if [ -z \"$username\" -o -z \"$password\" ]; then\n"
"    echo \"Username and password are required.\"\n"
"    exit 1\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"mkdir -m 0600 $SNAP_DATA/options\n"
"echo \"username: $username\" > $SNAP_DATA/options/credentials\n"
"echo \"password: $password\" >> $SNAP_DATA/options/credentials\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:106
msgid ""
"The same hook can also modify the configuration of a snap within the context "
"of the current transaction. This is accomplished using `snapctl set` and "
"`snapctl unset`. For more information see {ref}`Adding Snap configuration "
"<how-to-guides-manage-snaps-set-system-options>` and {ref}`Using the snapctl "
"tool <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-use-snapctl>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:108
msgid ""
"ⓘ Note that configuration options do not need to be defined anywhere. "
"`snapctl set` and `snap set` will accept any (valid) option name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:110
msgid "<span id=\"heading--default-configure\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:110
msgid "<span id=\"heading--default-configure\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:111
msgid "The default-configure hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:113
msgid ""
"The default-configure-hook is an optional extension to the {ref}`configure "
"hook <reference-development-supported-snap-hooks>` that executes only on "
"snap installation and _before_ services are started to provide access to the "
"default configuration values stored in a device’s {ref}`gadget snap "
"<reference-development-yaml-schemas-the-gadget-snap>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:115
msgid ""
"The default-configure hook should be located within `meta/hooks` and "
"requires a configure hook to be present. A missing configure hook will "
"result in an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:117
msgid ""
"The hook should use `snapctl get` to retrieve default configuration options "
"and `snapctl set` and `snapctl unset` to create/modify options. If the hook "
"exits with a non-zero status code, the default configuration provided by the "
"gadget snap as well as modifications by the hook will not be applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:119
msgid "Example default-configure hook:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:121
msgid ""
"#!/bin/sh -e\n"
"\n"
"DEFAULT_GADGET_OPTION=\"123\"\n"
"\n"
"gadget_option=\"$(snapctl get gadget-option)\"\n"
"if [ -z \"$gadget_option\" ]; then\n"
"gadget_option=\"$DEFAULT_GADGET_OPTION\"\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"mkdir -m 0600 $SNAP_DATA/options\n"
"echo \"option: $gadget_option\" > $SNAP_DATA/options/gadget\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:135
msgid ""
"For more information see {ref}`Adding Snap configuration <how-to-guides-"
"manage-snaps-set-system-options>` and {ref}`Using the snapctl tool <how-to-"
"guides-manage-snaps-use-snapctl>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:137
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:137
msgid "<span id=\"heading--fde\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:138
msgid "The full-disk-encryption hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:140
msgid ""
"[Ubuntu Core 20 ](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/uc20/) (UC20) uses [full disk "
"encryption](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/uc20/full-disk-encryption) (FDE) "
"whenever the hardware allows, protecting both the confidentiality and "
"integrity of a device’s data when there’s physical access to a device, or "
"after a device has been lost or stolen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:142
msgid ""
"Creating a verifiable boot process on a non-standard (non-UEFI+TPM platform) "
"FDE platform, such as a Raspberry Pi or other ARM devices, is board-specific "
"and will typically involve creating custom gadget and kernel snaps. UC20, "
"however, does provide a helper mechanism, via a hook interface, to ensure "
"the integrity of any subsequently executed or accessed data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:144
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Full-disk-encryption hooks <reference-development-uc20-fde-hooks>` "
"for details on how this hook is implemented.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:146
msgid "<span id=\"heading--gate-auto-refresh\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:146
msgid "<span id=\"heading--gate-auto-refresh\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:147
msgid "The gate-auto-refresh hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:149
msgid ""
"The gate-auto-refresh hook is executed by snapd for every snap that will be "
"updated with the next automatic refresh. It’s also executed for every snap "
"that is dependent on a snap that will be updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:151
msgid ""
"This hook is capable of executing the snapctl refresh command with 3 "
"specific arguments, hold, proceed and pending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:153
msgid ""
"This feature is currently considered experimental. See {ref}`Refresh control "
"<how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-manage-updates>` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:155
msgid "<span id=\"heading--install\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:155
msgid "<span id=\"heading--install\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:156
msgid "The install hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:158
msgid ""
"The `install` hook is called upon initial install only, i.e. it's not called "
"on subsequent refreshes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:160
msgid ""
"The hook is executed before starting snap services (if it has any) and "
"before the `configure` hook. The install hook is the place for one-time "
"actions, such as an early initialisation of a resource when installed for "
"the first time."
msgstr ""

