#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:170
msgid "The interface hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:172
msgid ""
"Interface hooks are executed when an interface is either connected or "
"disconnected via the interface’s plugs and slots mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:174
msgid ""
"They can be used to read or write attributes from a connection and, for "
"example, acquire new resources, update internal options or update databases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:176
msgid ""
"For further details, see {ref}`Interface hooks <explanation-interfaces-"
"interface-hooks>`."
msgstr ""

