#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:193
msgid "<span id=\"heading--pre-refresh\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:193
msgid "<span id=\"heading--pre-refresh\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:194
msgid "The pre-refresh hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:196
msgid "The `pre-refresh` hook is called whenever the snap gets refreshed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:198
msgid ""
"This hook is executed for the already installed revision of the snap with "
"its services still running (if the snap has any services) and before "
"switching to the newly installed revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:200
msgid ""
"This hook is a good place for any maintenance or cleanup actions that "
"prepare the snap for switching to the new revision. It's also a good place "
"to test whether a refresh will succeed,  because if the test causes the hook "
"to fail, the refresh will not proceed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:202
msgid ""
"The `pre-refresh` hook is not executed when {ref}`snap revert <tutorials-get-"
"started>` is used to install an earlier revision of a snap. If such an "
"operation affects snap functionality, the snap needs to detect this action "
"and manually perform whatever actions may be necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:204
msgid "<span id=\"heading--post-refresh\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:204
msgid "<span id=\"heading--post-refresh\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:205
msgid "The post-refresh hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:207
msgid ""
"The `post-refresh` hook is similar to `pre-refresh` (above) in that it is "
"called whenever the snap gets refreshed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:209
msgid ""
"This hook is executed for the newly installed revision of the snap, before "
"starting new services (if applicable). This hook is a good place for any "
"extra actions that need to be performed for the new revision of the snap. "
"It's also a good place to test whether a refresh has succeeded, because if "
"the test causes the hook to fail, the refresh will be rolled-back and the "
"original state of the snap restored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:211
msgid ""
"The `post-refresh` hook is not executed when {ref}`snap revert <tutorials-"
"get-started>` is used to install an earlier revision of a snap. If such an "
"operation affects snap functionality, the snap needs to detect this action "
"and manually perform whatever actions may be necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:213
msgid "<span id=\"heading--remove\"></span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:213
msgid "<span id=\"heading--remove\">"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:214
msgid "The remove hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:216
msgid ""
"The `remove` hook is called when the last revision of the snap gets removed "
"from the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/supported-snap-hooks.md:218
msgid ""
"This hook is executed after stopping the services of the snap (if the snap "
"has any services), therefore it's useful for any custom cleanup logic."
msgstr ""
